worth in a fight? Not very much, but a thousand of them are worth a lot. Well, if it's not that

01:12:34.450 --> 01:12:39.300
men in the county. Henry Dreiser has a hundred men in his Farmers Protective Association, and he's

01:12:39.300 --> 01:12:48.010
only 25% organized. How many people is that, Ed, figuring three to a family? Over a thousand. But

01:12:48.010 --> 01:12:53.200
suppose Riker drives these homesteaders away. I think you can discount that rumor. Well, you're not

01:12:53.200 --> 01:12:58.760
planning on tangling with them again, are you? There were people killed this afternoon. Makes my position

01:12:58.760 --> 01:12:59.800
pretty clear, doesn't it?

01:13:00.830 --> 01:13:09.590
Dan, when I sold Henry that wire, I didn't realize it would all come tumbling down on you.

01:13:10.310 --> 01:13:13.710
Funny. You never know who's going to fire the first shot until the fight begins.

01:13:14.180 --> 01:13:21.050
400 families. If each family spent, say, 500 dollars a year here in town, how much business would that come to?

01:13:21.440 --> 01:13:23.560
Almost. Almost a quarter million dollars.

01:13:23.820 --> 01:13:25.200
How much did the trail hands spend?

01:13:25.810 --> 01:13:29.670
Now, if 400 only spend...

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:34.160
hundred dollars a year. If, if, if, I know what I'm going to do, I'm going straight to

01:13:34.160 --> 01:13:38.940
Charlie and get word to Riker that Dan don't represent me. I am neutral. I don't want any

01:13:38.940 --> 01:13:46.310
part of this fight. Quiet. Suppose in a year from now, there are 800 families here. That's

01:13:46.310 --> 01:13:53.060
half a million dollars. Half a million dollars. And no shooting. But suppose the homesteaders

01:13:53.060 --> 01:13:53.860
are wiped out.

01:14:31.600 --> 01:14:32.700
Turn out the lights, Ned.

01:14:32.700 --> 01:14:34.070
Street's closed.

01:15:12.160 --> 01:15:25.790
You want me to turn to the men.

01:15:27.930 --> 01:15:28.770
Perhaps they can get together.

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:30.840
- Wait here.

01:15:32.850 --> 01:15:52.090
- Here, Jeff.

01:15:52.090 --> 01:15:54.030
- My people are mad, Dan.

01:15:54.030 --> 01:15:57.640
Everybody loved old man Hannaberry.

01:15:57.640 --> 01:15:59.390
- Evening, Marshal.

01:15:59.390 --> 01:16:00.000
- Evening, Jake.

01:16:01.600 --> 01:16:07.530
They want to settle this once and for all.

01:16:08.150 --> 01:16:09.150
Make this the last fight.

01:16:10.510 --> 01:16:11.710
I think it will be, Henry.

01:16:11.710 --> 01:16:17.570
I'm just brimming over with death

01:16:17.570 --> 01:16:21.050
Because I love it out in the West

01:16:21.050 --> 01:16:23.970
I love it out here in the West

01:16:23.970 --> 01:16:29.060
The West is in the dark dark

01:16:36.200 --> 01:16:37.280
That's why I love it.

01:16:37.460 --> 01:16:37.830
How about him?

01:16:38.580 --> 01:16:41.930
You sure would have looked nice in a kitchen apron.

01:16:43.310 --> 01:16:44.770
What do you mean stopping the show?

01:16:45.210 --> 01:16:47.290
I still own this place, and I'll give the orders.

01:16:47.910 --> 01:16:48.570
That's fair enough.

01:16:48.650 --> 01:16:49.630
Tell him to turn out the lights.

01:16:51.320 --> 01:16:52.000
Grab him, boys.

01:16:52.220 --> 01:16:52.740
Look out there!

01:16:57.590 --> 01:16:58.310
Lights out, Charlie.

01:17:01.080 --> 01:17:13.670
- You want me to do it for you? - You'll set the police on fire.

01:17:13.720 --> 01:17:22.600
- I wouldn't want to do that. - Wait. Lights out.

01:17:48.780 --> 01:17:59.920
tell you to pack up. Maybe breaking it up is a better idea. I'm breaking nothing. You're not closing me up. Listen Rita. It's going to be pretty rough here in no time. Not safe. Oh don't you tell me what safe.

01:18:00.190 --> 01:18:02.290
You big blonde baboon, don't you warn me.

01:18:02.290 --> 01:18:03.630
You wait till Riker gets here.

01:18:03.630 --> 01:18:04.430
You warn me?

01:18:04.430 --> 01:18:05.190
Seemed only friendly.

01:18:05.190 --> 01:18:06.570
I'd do the same for you.

01:18:06.570 --> 01:18:07.430
The jig's up.

01:18:07.430 --> 01:18:08.270
It sure is.

01:18:08.270 --> 01:18:09.780
But not for me.

01:18:09.780 --> 01:18:11.890
Who's going to stand with you when the shooting starts?

01:18:11.890 --> 01:18:12.810
The merchants?

01:18:12.810 --> 01:18:14.040
The homesteaders?

01:18:14.040 --> 01:18:15.700
Why, you'll be so lonely on that street

01:18:15.700 --> 01:18:18.320
you'll look like a duck in a shooting gallery.

01:18:18.320 --> 01:18:20.470
The tame always win, Rita.

01:18:20.470 --> 01:18:22.730
This place will fall around your lovely ears,

01:18:22.730 --> 01:18:25.390
dollar by dollar, dime by dime.

01:18:25.390 --> 01:18:27.550
Get out of here before I kill you.

01:18:27.550 --> 01:18:29.160
And I don't mean half kill you.

01:18:29.160 --> 01:18:30.000
This is my property.

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:31.240
Paid for with my money.

01:18:31.240 --> 01:18:33.000
And if you ever set foot inside this room again,

01:18:33.000 --> 01:18:35.640
I'll waste your brains out from brainless idiots.

01:18:35.640 --> 01:18:44.870
Suppose 1,000 families only spend $300 a year.

01:18:44.870 --> 01:18:45.750
Yeah, they come.

01:19:01.790 --> 01:19:03.000
Hey, Cap, look.

01:19:06.320 --> 01:19:10.140
What's the idea of the saloon's being closed?

01:19:10.650 --> 01:19:12.230
New law went into effect tonight.

01:19:13.730 --> 01:19:15.130
Do you think you can stop us?

01:19:16.070 --> 01:19:18.320
You got a pretty strong outfit.

01:19:21.030 --> 01:19:24.820
Boys, anybody want to get the trail dust out of their throats?

01:19:42.730 --> 01:19:45.330
It won't take them long to get licked up and start on this side of the street.

01:19:47.210 --> 01:19:48.360
Hey, Cap, come back!

01:19:49.140 --> 01:19:51.180
I'm sure glad to see you.

01:19:51.380 --> 01:19:52.480
Let him close you up, did you?

01:19:52.780 --> 01:19:54.080
Oh, now, Cap, look!

01:19:55.320 --> 01:19:57.060
All right, boys.

01:19:57.460 --> 01:19:57.860
Take it!

01:19:58.060 --> 01:19:58.560
Let's go!

01:19:58.560 --> 01:19:58.900
Let's go!

01:20:14.910 --> 01:20:15.910
Are they coming?

01:20:15.910 --> 01:20:16.730
I hope so.

01:20:16.730 --> 01:20:19.770
But if they don't get here soon, they'll be too late.

01:20:19.770 --> 01:20:21.770
I understand you told them about selling us the wire.

01:20:21.770 --> 01:20:24.010
And that you believe in what we're trying to do.

01:20:24.010 --> 01:20:28.450
I believe in you.

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:32.000
Can a cattleman show you how?

01:20:32.000 --> 01:20:34.780
What do you mean?

01:20:34.780 --> 01:20:46.600
Nice work.

01:20:46.600 --> 01:20:48.600
I've been eating so hard.

01:20:48.600 --> 01:20:53.160
How do you feel?

01:20:53.160 --> 01:20:55.150
Fine. Oh, Dan.

01:20:55.150 --> 01:20:58.160
Sherry, I'm proud of.

01:20:58.160 --> 01:21:00.000
I'm proud of you, Dan. And Henry.

01:21:00.920 --> 01:21:01.640
Me, too.

01:21:02.440 --> 01:21:03.700
It's getting pretty rough down there, man.

01:21:03.920 --> 01:21:04.580
Can't you stop it?

01:21:04.680 --> 01:21:07.080
She's a wonderful girl, Henry, and you'd better get her out of here

01:21:07.080 --> 01:21:09.400
before I change my mind and take her away from you.

01:21:09.680 --> 01:21:10.280
Take her away?

01:21:10.790 --> 01:21:11.230
You mean you...

01:21:11.230 --> 01:21:11.610
Exactly.

01:21:14.360 --> 01:21:16.010
Come on, Henry.

01:21:16.360 --> 01:21:17.520
I'll explain it to you.

01:21:17.520 --> 01:21:18.880
Come on.

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:30.840
- What are you doing out there?

01:21:30.840 --> 01:21:33.290
- Well, somebody's got to protect the sheriff's office.

01:21:33.290 --> 01:21:34.690
Where are you fixin' to go?

01:21:34.690 --> 01:21:35.750
- Every fella over at Causeville

01:21:35.750 --> 01:21:36.710
has been loosing some sheep.

01:21:36.710 --> 01:21:39.750
He wanted me to be investigated for his chance ahead.

01:21:39.750 --> 01:21:54.330
- Hm, sheep.

01:21:54.330 --> 01:21:55.870
- You're makin' a mistake, Henry.

01:21:55.870 --> 01:21:58.890
Why should we help a town that don't want any part of us?

01:21:58.890 --> 01:22:00.000
- What's the matter, afraid?

01:22:00.190 --> 01:22:01.890
No, ma'am. We're not afraid.

01:22:01.890 --> 01:22:04.290
We just don't quite know what this is all about.

01:22:04.290 --> 01:22:05.480
Well, then I'll tell you.

01:22:05.480 --> 01:22:09.310
It's about drunken trailhands that don't want you to settle the land that's yours.

01:22:09.310 --> 01:22:11.220
It's about farms and homes.

01:22:11.220 --> 01:22:13.720
And it's about a fool marshal who's got himself in a corner

01:22:13.720 --> 01:22:17.520
because he knows better times are coming if the people only have the nerve to do their part.

01:22:17.520 --> 01:22:18.420
In this town?

01:22:18.420 --> 01:22:20.220
It's not this town you're fighting for.

01:22:20.220 --> 01:22:21.120
It's the right to live.

01:22:21.120 --> 01:22:22.510
What's going on here?

01:22:22.510 --> 01:22:24.540
You say this town wants no part of you.

01:22:24.540 --> 01:22:26.940
Why, here's Sheriff Trimble, come to lead you.

01:22:26.940 --> 01:22:27.440
What's that?

01:22:27.440 --> 01:22:29.730
Must be at least 300 votes in these homesteaders.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:31.380
I got to see a man about a sheep.

01:22:32.020 --> 01:22:34.340
You're the sheriff that captured Jett Younger, aren't you?

01:22:35.000 --> 01:22:35.360
Yeah.

01:22:35.580 --> 01:22:36.820
What the hell I had a hand in it?

01:22:37.260 --> 01:22:38.920
Well, we'll follow you, Sheriff.

01:22:39.180 --> 01:22:39.920
Come on, boys.

01:22:39.920 --> 01:22:40.340
Come on.

01:23:00.090 --> 01:23:06.350
You know, Doug, the world is changing.

01:23:07.340 --> 01:23:08.650
Yeah, I know.

01:23:09.440 --> 01:23:15.330
Glory, glory, hallelujah.

01:23:15.330 --> 01:23:28.820
You're here, boys.

01:23:29.100 --> 01:23:29.900
What do you want us to do, Marshal?

01:23:30.350 --> 01:23:34.270
fan out they got positions around the stores and buildings on that side of the street here

01:23:34.270 --> 01:23:40.120
the fellas spread out on that side over there boys on that road what's ryker's men up to now

01:23:40.630 --> 01:23:44.180
having the time of their lives wiping out the saloons and gambling houses

01:23:44.180 --> 01:23:54.900
and you ain't doing nothing about it not me they're doing too good a job this year sure is

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:32.950
You're the man that wanted an open town.

01:24:32.950 --> 01:24:34.950
Well, here it is, Charlie. Wide open.

01:24:34.950 --> 01:24:37.950
- Circle bar! - Johnny Jones, circle bar!

01:24:37.950 --> 01:24:40.400
- Circle bar! - Johnny Jones, circle bar!

01:25:23.200 --> 01:25:30.000
When I have I'll find more somewhere else. Tell you boys if they try to cross the street they'll find armed men

01:25:30.090 --> 01:25:35.710
waiting for them I'll take my boys anywhere I want to go you're not taking

01:25:35.710 --> 01:25:44.760
them anywhere like are you coming with me I am yes you're under arrest the

01:25:44.760 --> 01:25:46.840
charge is murder

01:26:14.240 --> 01:26:17.220
We'll eat from now on, I'll catch you later.

01:26:35.760 --> 01:27:00.000
I doing we've had enough trouble it's over now where's cap where's right

01:27:00.000 --> 01:27:00.830
Riker.

01:27:00.830 --> 01:27:04.140
Riker's dead, and so is your part of Abilene.

01:27:04.140 --> 01:27:06.140
All that's left of it is the trail back.

01:27:06.140 --> 01:27:10.080
Boys, this is the way a tough street dies.

01:27:10.080 --> 01:27:13.680
Not with a roar, but with a whine.

01:27:13.680 --> 01:27:16.070
You don't want to die here with it.

01:27:16.070 --> 01:27:20.980
The tame are taking over Abilene, and they're tougher than you think.

01:27:20.980 --> 01:27:21.980
Better ride, boys.

01:27:21.980 --> 01:27:22.960
Now's our chance.

01:27:22.960 --> 01:27:23.960
Drive 'em out of town.

01:27:23.960 --> 01:27:24.960
Get 'em, boys.

01:27:24.960 --> 01:27:25.850
The fight's over.

01:27:25.850 --> 01:27:29.250
Let 'em ride out of town.

01:27:42.190 --> 01:27:46.200
I don't know whether you joined us or we joined you, but it's good to be together.

01:28:06.330 --> 01:28:07.330
We sure done it.

01:28:16.110 --> 01:28:25.690
Remember one thing.

01:28:26.050 --> 01:28:26.770
No beer.

01:28:29.130 --> 01:28:30.000
You don't want to.

01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:31.300
- That's what I was thinking, Annie.

01:28:31.300 --> 01:28:34.570
- That there's time for one game of Phan-Tan.

01:28:38.900 --> 01:28:49.450
- Hey, you play Phan-Tan?

01:28:49.450 --> 01:28:53.350
How about little Phan-Tan?

01:28:53.350 --> 01:28:55.320
Just one little game, Annie.
